# r92-b research-only instrumentation: MLX generated-MSL verbose dump
#
# Base:      8486638578a283de40369172f68c3a4d2d6a5365 (codex/mlxfast-maple-20260804-advisor)
# Generated: git diff <base> -- Sources/MLXFastModel/ (final instrumented state,
#            i.e. the exact tree that produced BOTH the Stage 1 oracle dump and
#            the Stage 1' scored-path dump).
# Sites:     48 MLXFastKernel.callAsFunction invocations across three files -- every
#            `outputDTypes:` argument. None of these files uses `initValue:` or
#            `stream:`, so `outputDTypes:` is always the last labelled argument
#            and `verbose:` goes immediately after it.
#              Sources/MLXFastModel/LagunaRuntimeModel.swift   33
#              Sources/MLXFastModel/LagunaRuntimeLayers.swift   9
#              Sources/MLXFastModel/LagunaLmHeadPrune.swift     6
#
# Every site is `verbose: lagunaR92Verbose()`, not `verbose: true`. The helper
# and its two supporting globals are added near the top of
# Sources/MLXFastModel/LagunaRuntimeModel.swift:
#
#   lagunaR92DumpRedirect   env DARKBLOOM_R92_DUMP_TO_STDERR=1 ->
#                           dup2(STDERR_FILENO, STDOUT_FILENO) + setvbuf, so the
#                           dump survives the runtime worker, which nulls stdout
#                           but not stderr (RuntimeWorkerProtocolIO
#                           .isolatingStandardIO, LagunaRuntimeWorker.swift
#                           :1187-1203). Emits one R92CANARY line.
#   LagunaR92DumpBudget     NSLock-guarded emission counter, limit from env
#                           DARKBLOOM_R92_DUMP_LIMIT (default 900), PER WORKER
#                           PROCESS. Without it the scored run writes tens of GB.
#   lagunaR92Verbose()      true while the budget is unspent.
#
# Only the local-iterate / local-submit benchmark forwards worker stderr
# (forwardsWorkerStderr, Sources/MLXFastCLI/main.swift:315-318 vs the
# `= false` default at :1239-1319), which is why the scored dump has to go
# through ./benchmark.sh and not through `mlxfast-swift correctness`.
#
# Re-apply from a clean checkout at that base:
#   git apply research/maple-frieren-r92-verbose-dump.patch
# The 48 call-site edits alone (with `verbose: true`) can also be regenerated
# line-number-independently:
#   python3 senpai/tools/agx-census-probe/add_verbose_dump.py
#
# RELOCATION WARNING: this diff carries absolute line numbers into files that
# every experiment edits. If `git apply` rejects, do NOT hand-fix the hunks --
# rerun add_verbose_dump.py and re-add the three globals by hand.
#
# NOT A SUBMISSION CANDIDATE. `verbose:` makes MLX print the fully generated MSL
# to std::cout at every kernel op construction
# (Vendor/mlx-swift/Source/Cmlx/mlx/mlx/backend/common/metal_kernel.cpp:343),
# which is pure host-side I/O on the scored hot path; it cost 42.9 % of the
# local est score in the Stage 1' run. It is reverted in the final commit of
# this branch and contributes zero editable bytes to the submitted surface.
